(DharmaAI - Mahabharata Demo Knowledge Base) Tj
T* (Original educational summary prepared for this demonstration.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The Pandavas) Tj
T* (The five Pandava brothers are Yudhishthira, Bhima, Arjuna, Nakula,) Tj
T* (and Sahadeva. Yudhishthira is the eldest and is associated with) Tj
T* (truth and justice. Bhima is known for strength. Arjuna is a skilled) Tj
T* (archer. Nakula and Sahadeva are the youngest brothers.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Krishna and Arjuna) Tj
T* (Before the battle at Kurukshetra, Arjuna hesitates to fight his) Tj
T* (relatives and teachers. Krishna serves as his charioteer and guide.) Tj
T* (Krishna teaches Arjuna to act with responsibility and discipline,) Tj
T* (without becoming attached to the rewards of his actions. These) Tj
T* (teachings form the dialogue known as the Bhagavad Gita.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Karna) Tj
T* (Karna is a gifted warrior and the son of Kunti. Raised by a) Tj
T* (charioteer family, he faces rejection because of his social status.) Tj
T* (Duryodhana offers him friendship and recognition. Karna remains) Tj
T* (loyal to Duryodhana despite learning his connection to the Pandavas.) Tj
T* (His conflict between loyalty, identity, and duty makes him tragic.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (The conflict and its lessons) Tj
T* (The war follows a struggle over the kingdom between the Pandavas) Tj
T* (and the Kauravas. The dice game, the humiliation of Draupadi, exile,) Tj
T* (and failed negotiations deepen the conflict. Draupadi challenges) Tj
T* (injustice and asks difficult questions about power and dignity.) Tj
T* (The epic explores duty, justice, loyalty, and the cost of ambition.) Tj
T* (It shows that moral choices can be difficult and have consequences.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Scope of this knowledge base) Tj
T* (This short document covers only the characters and themes above.) Tj
T* (It contains no recipes, stock prices, or software installation advice.) Tj
